  The reel_script and caption say the fraud victims were 'இழப்பு' of Rs 4.59 lakh in Pollachi; the article says the frauds occurred across the Coimbatore district, and the headline's 'பொள்ளாச்சி' location tag is an over-generalization since Periyanaickenpalayam and Kaniyur are separate areas (the tamil_headline and slides_spec 'loc' attribute all three cases to Pollachi).
  The reel_script says the 64-year-old businessman sent money to a 'பஞ்சாப் நிறுவனம்' (Punjab company); the article says the company is in Ludhiana, which is in Punjab, so this is acceptable, but the reel_script omits that the company is in Ludhiana (minor detail).
  The reel_script states the victim with the credit card was told to pay a 'பதிவுக் கட்டணம்' only implicitly; the article says he was asked to download the 'ஷைன் ஜாப் ஹைரிங்' app and pay the registration fee through a credit card, and the reel_script omits the app detail, which is an important way of the fraud.
  The reel_script says the 44-year-old's bank money was taken after he entered Aadhaar and phone number, but omits that the fake message was from a 'ஆர்.டி.ஓ. போக்குவரத்து அபராதச் சீட்டு' (RTO traffic fine slip), which is the key cause and is only partially conveyed.
  The reel_script and caption say the 41-year-old was a 'வேலை தேடுபவர்' and the caller said he was a private company employee, which the draft omits; not a fabrication but a missing detail of the scam mechanism.
  The caption says the 41-year-old was asked to pay 'பதிவுக் கட்டணம்' by credit card, which matches the article, but the caption's 'பெரியநாயக்கன்பாளையத்தைச் சேர்ந்த 44 வயது நபர்... ஆதார், கைப்பேசி எண்ணைப் பதிவு செய்ததால்' attributes a cause ('ததால்') that the article gives, so this is fine; however the caption states the 64-year-old businessman's order was 'கடந்த மாதம் 29ஆம் தேதி' which the article gives, so no problem there.
